---
// Exterior house washing — a LEAF page under the Home Cleaning mega-menu's
// third group, "Outside your home" (navigation.ts). Last of the five in that
// group to be built, alongside window, gutter, roof and high pressure.
//
// It is the widest of the five and it is the one that sells the other four,
// so its job is to describe the whole outside of a house and then hand the
// reader off honestly. Its middle uses `CardCarousel`, which no other page in
// this group uses, because the three cards here are one idea shown three ways
// (the film, the wall without it, the person who does it) rather than three
// different purchases.
//
// ⚠️ OVERLAP TO WATCH. This page and /house-cleaning/pressure-cleaning/ can end up
// competing, since both mention walls. The line held here: THIS page is
// vertical surfaces, by soft wash, at low pressure. THAT page is the ground
// and hard surfaces, by force. Each says so and each links the other. And
// /house-cleaning/mould-removal/ is INSIDE the house, which is a different
// service with a health dimension; it is linked from §4 rather than competed
// with.
//
// NO CONTENT BRIEF EXISTS for any of the five. All copy below is DRAFTED, not
// supplied, and needs sign-off. Facts only TLB holds ship as [brackets].
//
// BLOCKS LAUNCH:
//   - IS THIS DELIVERED IN HOUSE? Soft washing a whole house needs a low
//     pressure unit, the right chemistry and enough reach for a two-storey
//     wall. If it is subcontracted, §8's comparison table ("employed by TLB,
//     not subcontracted") contradicts the page and comes off it.
//   - WHAT SOLUTION, AT WHAT DILUTION, AND WHAT ABOUT THE GARDEN? Bracketed
//     in §5 and branded FAQ 3. This is the biggest complaint risk on the
//     page, exactly as it is on the roof page, and one answer fixes both.
//   - PAINTED SURFACES AND WARRANTIES. §5 says we do not use enough pressure
//     to strip sound paint. Confirm, and confirm what TLB says about walls
//     that are already flaking, because that is the argument that follows a
//     complaint.
//   - HOW HIGH? A two-storey wall and a gable end over a garden bed is the
//     job that tests it. Bracketed in branded FAQ 4.
//   - ASBESTOS. Older fibre cement cladding and eave sheeting is the same
//     issue as the roof page's, and non-branded FAQ 4 says we do not touch
//     it. This must match TLB's actual policy.
//   - PRICING BASIS and minimum charge. Bracketed in non-branded FAQ 5.
//   - [insured] in §4 card 3 is inherited from the commercial hub.
//
// PHOTOGRAPHY: four generated assets of its own in
// src/assets/home_cleaning/outside_your_home/exterior_house_washing/, prompts
// in the IMAGE-PROMPTS.md beside them, plus the cluster's shared backdrop one
// level up.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/sections/SiteHeader.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/sections/Hero.astro';
import TrustBar from '../../components/sections/TrustBar.astro';
import Backdrop from '../../components/ui/Backdrop.astro';
import TextBlock from '../../components/sections/TextBlock.astro';
import CardCarousel from '../../components/sections/CardCarousel.astro';
import ServiceBlocks from '../../components/sections/ServiceBlocks.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/sections/Callout.astro';
import BeforeAfter from '../../components/sections/BeforeAfter.astro';
import ComparisonTable from '../../components/sections/ComparisonTable.astro';
import GoogleReviewSlider from '../../components/sections/GoogleReviewSlider.astro';
import { googleBusinessProfileUrl, googleReviews } from '../../data/googleReviews';
import TagCloud from '../../components/sections/TagCloud.astro';
import Faq from '../../components/sections/Faq.astro';
import CallToAction from '../../components/sections/CallToAction.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/sections/SiteFooter.astro';
import logoImg from '../../assets/logo/tlb-logo-horizontal.png';
import footerLogoImg from '../../assets/logo/tlb-logo-square.png';
// Shared across all five pages in this group. See the window page's note.
// SAMPLE illustrations, not photographs. See §6.
import {
  primaryNav,
  headerNav,
  headerSecondaryCta,
  footerServiceLinks,
  footerContact,
  footerCopyright,
  quoteCta,
} from '../../data/navigation';
import { comparisonColumns, comparisonRows } from '../../data/comparison';
import { locationGroups } from '../../data/locations';
import { trustBarCards } from '../../data/trust';
import { otherOutsideServices } from '../../data/outsideYourHome';
import { howItWorks, managedForYou, theLineBody } from '../../data/brand-lines';
import { localBusiness } from '../../data/business';
import { z } from 'astro/zod';
import { getPage } from '../../lib/cms';
import * as section from '../../lib/cms-schemas';
import { sized } from '../../lib/cms-schemas';

// §0 Metadata. "House washing", "exterior cleaning" and "soft wash" are the
// synonyms; the first two are now settled in the opening paragraph and the
// third is carried in body copy.
//
// Title and description are the SIGNED-OFF workbook text (Keyword Mapping &
// Metadata, sheet 1 row 17), reproduced verbatim. The old title said "Washing"
// where the mapped primary `exterior house cleaning` (450/mo) says "Cleaning";
// the old description ran 23 characters over the limit and carried the mapped
// phrase nowhere.
//
// ⚠️ NOT BLOCKING, but it affects this page more than any other in the batch.
// The workbook maps `exterior house cleaning` as the primary while its own
// Page column says "Exterior house washing", the URL says
// `exterior-house-washing`, and every heading on the live page said "washing"
// too. Washing and cleaning are not variants of each other for the
// contiguous-phrase test, so one word was costing five of the eight
// primary-keyword components. The headings below fix that; the URL cannot be
// fixed, because Rule 2 makes the signed-off workbook URL the target. So this
// page will always carry a slug that does not contain its own primary keyword.
//
// TWO WAYS OUT, both for the workbook owner rather than for copy: change the
// mapped primary to a washing term, which needs a live volume check, or accept
// the URL as a permanent partial miss and keep the cleaning primary in the
// headings. The second is what this file implements, because the approved
// title also uses "Cleaning" and consistency with the signed-off title matters
// more than the slug.
//
// In `pageMeta`, on `canonical`:
// ⚠️ Placeholder domain, same as every sibling page. Confirm before launch.

// The page's one primary CTA, per BFD 9.5, repeated on every in-page button.
// `Book a house wash today` is the approved workbook CTA and it fits a button
// at 23 characters, so it goes on unchanged. It is also the one approved CTA
// of the five exterior pages that reads naturally and promises nothing the
// page cannot keep.
//
// It resolves a BFD 13.2 conflict: the old `Get an instant quote` promised
// instant pricing on a page whose own pricing block says the honest answer is
// a fast quote, and whose last FAQ says the price moves with storeys, growth,
// wall material and what else is being done at the same time.
//
// The header keeps the site-wide quoteCta — that is chrome, not this page.
const pageCta = { ...quoteCta, label: 'Book a house wash today' };

// §1 Hero. The H1 now carries the mapped primary `exterior house cleaning`
// (450/mo) as an exact contiguous phrase. The extension is the PROBLEM rather
// than the region, because this page's buyer is diagnosing a discolouration
// rather than searching for a local trade, and the region is already in the
// lead. The old heading — the realisation this service depends on, that people
// stop seeing their own walls because the change happened a shade at a time
// over about five years — is the best hero line of the eight and is not cut:
// it opens the lead, because its whole effect depends on the second fragment
// landing alone.
//
// The subheading is a NEW line. Its extension is the method promise rather
// than the H1's problem list, and it puts the surface-first argument above the
// fold, which is what §3's "Where we stop" and the flaking-paint FAQ both rest
// on. H1, subheading and the coverage H2 are taken from the worked-example
// table in references/h1-patterns.md, which covers this exact workbook row.
//
// The mapped phrase is NOT repeated a third time in the lead: the H1 and
// subheading directly above both carry it and a third exact instance in the
// prose beneath them would read as filler.
//
// Scene photo, family A, square source so the 1/1 box crops nothing.

// §2 Definition. The answer target. Paragraph two is the fact the whole page
// turns on and the reason people are surprised by the result: what is on the
// wall is mostly alive, so it is not paint fade and it is not permanent.
//
// In `definitionBody`, on its first paragraph:
// Opens with the mapped primary as a contiguous phrase — the opening
// paragraph is scored on the first two sentences — and naming both terms in
// the first clause resolves the synonym for the reader, which the window and
// high pressure pages both do well and this one did not.

// §3 What it is. `CardCarousel`, whose cards take an image plus a heading and
// body. Used here and nowhere else in this group: three cards that are one
// argument shown three ways, which is what a centre-emphasis carousel is
// good at, and it keeps this page from opening like the four beside it.

// §4 What the wash covers. `ServiceBlocks` icon grid. Six items, and the order
// is the order of the job: top down, because anything else means washing the
// same wall twice.
//
// ⚠️ EVERY ITEM IS DRAFTED against ordinary practice, not supplied by TLB.
// Confirm each and cut what TLB does not do. Three carry blockers, marked.
//
// In `scopeItems`, on the description of "Low pressure and a solution":
// ⚠️ BLOCKER. Confirm the product and dilution. Same question as the
// roof page's, and one answer fixes both.
// In `scopeItems`, on the description of "Plants, pets and furniture":
// ⚠️ BLOCKER, and the biggest complaint risk on the page.

// §5 The note. `Callout` `note` tone rather than `warning`, because this is
// the "worth knowing" moment rather than the "do not do this" one: the
// warning about high pressure is already made in full on the high pressure
// page, and repeating it here at the same volume would be the site arguing
// with itself.
//
// ⚠️ VERIFY THE WORDING. Mould and algae being living growth that regrows
// from what is left behind is standard, and it is the reason a treated wall
// stays clean longer than a blasted one. Stated with no product named and no
// duration promised.

// §6 Before and after. SAMPLE illustrations, not photographs. See the window
// page's §6 note, which applies verbatim.
//
// THE PHOTO BRIEF for a real pair: one wall, ideally a shaded elevation with
// visible growth, shot from a fixed tripod position, before and after, with
// nothing moved between the frames and at the same time of day so the shadow
// line matches. Include the eaves and one window in the frame, because those
// are the parts the copy promises and the parts a reader checks.

// §7 When to book it. Short dark block. Doubles as the section that explains
// the right ORDER for the whole outside of a house, which is the single most
// useful thing this page can tell someone who is about to book three services
// from this group.

// §8 The rest of the cluster. Shared data, this page's own href filtered out.
const siblingItems = otherOutsideServices('/house-cleaning/exterior-house-washing/');

// §9 Comparison table. Shared rows from src/data/comparison.ts.
//
// ⚠️ CONDITIONAL. Row one is "employed by TLB, not subcontracted". If this is
// subcontracted, the table contradicts the page and comes off it.

// §11 Branded FAQs, in the customer's voice. Self-contained 40 to 80 word
// answers, per BFD 3.5.
//
// In `brandedFaqItems`, on the answer to "Will it strip our paint?":
// ⚠️ BLOCKER. Confirm the position on already flaking paint.
// In `brandedFaqItems`, on the answer to "What about our garden?":
// ⚠️ BLOCKER. Same question as the roof page's. See §4.
// In `brandedFaqItems`, on the answer to "Can you reach a two-storey wall and the gable?":
// ⚠️ BLOCKER. Confirm the real cut-off. See the file header.

// §12 Non-branded FAQs.
//
// ⚠️ VERIFICATION PASS REQUIRED:
//   - Mould and algae as living growth on the surface, regrowing from
//     residue, is standard and correct.
//   - Soft washing versus high pressure, and which surfaces take which, is
//     standard practice and matches manufacturer care guidance for render,
//     prepainted steel and weatherboard.
//   - ⚠️ ASBESTOS. The answer below states we do not wash old fibre cement
//     cladding. This must match TLB's actual policy before publishing, and it
//     is worded as a referral rather than as advice.
//   - Frequency is hedged as an observation with shade and salt as the
//     variables.
//   - Pricing bracketed on purpose.
//
// In `nonBrandedFaqItems`, on the answer to "Can old fibre cement cladding be washed?":
// ⚠️ MUST MATCH TLB'S ACTUAL POLICY. See the note above this array.
// In `nonBrandedFaqItems`, on the answer to "How much does exterior house washing cost?":
// ⚠️ BRACKETED ON PURPOSE.

// §13 Closing CTA.

// CONTENT lives in src/content/pages/house-cleaning/exterior-house-washing.yaml
// and is edited in Pages CMS ("Exterior house washing", under House cleaning).
// This file owns the layout. The notes above explain why each section says
// what it says; they stay here because Pages CMS rewrites the YAML on save and
// would drop them.
const page = await getPage(
  'house-cleaning/exterior-house-washing',
  z.object({
    seo: section.seo,
    hero: section.hero,
    // Its background photo sits behind the trust bar and this block together
    // (the Backdrop below), so it cannot be left empty.
    definition: section.textBlock.extend({ backgroundImage: section.backgroundPhoto }),
    carousel: section.cardCarousel,
    scope: section.iconGrid,
    softWash: section.callout,
    beforeAfter: section.beforeAfter,
    order: section.textBlock,
    // Heading and lead only: the rows are the other outside pages, from the
    // shared cross-link list.
    outside: section.sectionIntro,
    // The table's columns and rows are the shared comparison table.
    comparison: section.comparisonTable.omit({ columns: true, rows: true }),
    reviews: section.sectionHeading,
    whereWeClean: section.tagCloud,
    // Heading only: the paragraphs under it all come from Brand lines.
    brandLine: section.sectionHeading,
    faq: section.faq,
    nonBrandedFaq: section.faq,
    closingCta: section.callToAction,
  }),
);

const pageMeta = {
  ...page.seo,
  // ⚠️ Placeholder domain, same as every sibling page. Confirm before launch.
  canonical: 'https://tlbcleaning.com.au/house-cleaning/exterior-house-washing/',
};

const business = localBusiness({
  description: pageMeta.description,
  areaServed: 'Northern Rivers NSW, the Tweed and Southern Gold Coast QLD',
  sameAs: googleBusinessProfileUrl ? [googleBusinessProfileUrl] : [],
});

const heroImage = page.hero.image && sized(page.hero.image, '1/1');

const carouselCards = page.carousel.cards.map((card) => ({
  ...card,
  image: card.image && sized(card.image, '4/3'),
}));
---

<Base title={pageMeta.title} description={pageMeta.description} canonical={pageMeta.canonical} business={business}>
  <SiteHeader
    logo={{ label: 'TLB Cleaning', src: logoImg }}
    primaryNav={primaryNav}
    serviceNav={headerNav}
    secondaryCta={headerSecondaryCta}
    cta={quoteCta}
  />

  <main id="main">
    <Hero
      variant="split-single-image"
      imagePosition="right"
      kicker={page.hero.kicker}
      headingLines={page.hero.headingLines}
      subheading={page.hero.subheading}
      lead={page.hero.lead}
      cta={page.hero.cta ?? pageCta}
      image={heroImage}
    />

    <Backdrop image={page.definition.backgroundImage} tint="muted" opacity={90} focus="bottom">
      <TrustBar variant="card" cards={trustBarCards} />
      <TextBlock
        theme="muted"
        align="left"
        heading={page.definition.heading}
        body={page.definition.body}
        cta={page.definition.cta}
      />
    </Backdrop>

    <CardCarousel
      heading={page.carousel.heading}
      lead={page.carousel.lead}
      cards={carouselCards}
    />

    <ServiceBlocks
      variant="icon-grid"
      heading={page.scope.heading}
      lead={page.scope.lead}
      note={page.scope.note}
      items={page.scope.items}
      cta={pageCta}
    />

    <Callout tone="note" heading={page.softWash.heading} body={page.softWash.body} cta={page.softWash.cta} />

    <BeforeAfter
      heading={page.beforeAfter.heading}
      lead={page.beforeAfter.lead}
      pairs={page.beforeAfter.pairs}
      note={page.beforeAfter.note}
      beforeLabel={page.beforeAfter.beforeLabel}
      afterLabel={page.beforeAfter.afterLabel}
    />

    <TextBlock
      theme="dark"
      align="left"
      heading={page.order.heading}
      body={page.order.body}
      cta={page.order.cta ?? pageCta}
      backgroundImage={page.order.backgroundImage}
    />

    <ServiceBlocks
      variant="list"
      heading={page.outside.heading}
      lead={page.outside.lead}
      items={siblingItems}
    />

    <ComparisonTable
      heading={page.comparison.heading}
      cornerLabel={page.comparison.cornerLabel}
      lead={page.comparison.lead}
      columns={comparisonColumns}
      rows={comparisonRows}
      footnote={page.comparison.footnote}
      cta={page.comparison.cta}
    />

    <GoogleReviewSlider heading={page.reviews.heading} reviews={googleReviews} profileUrl={googleBusinessProfileUrl} />

    <TagCloud
      heading={page.whereWeClean.heading}
      subheading={page.whereWeClean.subheading}
      tags={page.whereWeClean.tags}
      groups={locationGroups}
      note={page.whereWeClean.note}
    />

    {/* §1.3 The Line as a section heading, with §1.4 as its standfirst.
        The copy, and the reason this page gets `fast` rather than the other
        variant, both live in data/brand-lines.ts. Change it there, not here.

        `muted`, not `dark`: TagCloud above paints --color-brand and Faq below
        paints --color-surface, so Cream between them keeps the page
        alternating instead of stacking two dark bands.

        No CTA prop. §9.5 wants one primary CTA per page, repeated, and the
        closing CallToAction is directly under the FAQs. */}
    <TextBlock
      theme="muted"
      align="left"
      heading={page.brandLine.heading}
      body={[managedForYou.oneOff, ...theLineBody.residential, ...howItWorks.general]}
    />

    {/* The first FAQ heading renamed: these five are about paint, duration,
        gardens, reach and interior mould, all pre-booking questions. It also
        matches the approved CTA, `Book a house wash today`, so the heading and
        the button reinforce each other, and it keeps the exact primary out of
        a fourth slot. The second heading stays: it carries the "washing" form
        that the URL and the page name both use and that the new headings above
        no longer do, so it is the one place that phrasing survives in the body
        structure — and it is not a fourth instance of the mapped primary,
        because it says "washing" rather than "cleaning". */}
    <Faq heading={page.faq.heading} lead={page.faq.lead} items={page.faq.items} />
    <Faq heading={page.nonBrandedFaq.heading} lead={page.nonBrandedFaq.lead} items={page.nonBrandedFaq.items} />

    <CallToAction
      variant="secondary"
      kicker={page.closingCta.kicker}
      heading={page.closingCta.heading}
      lead={page.closingCta.lead}
      cta={page.closingCta.cta ?? pageCta}
    />
  </main>

  <SiteFooter
    logo={{ label: 'TLB Cleaning', src: footerLogoImg }}
    columns={[
      { title: 'Services', links: footerServiceLinks },
      { title: 'Locations', links: [{ label: 'View all locations', href: '/locations/' }] },
    ]}
    contact={footerContact}
    copyright={footerCopyright}
  />
</Base>
